# PowerPoint files stay out of git.
#
# This repo is deliberately all-text — HTML, CSS, JS, markdown — so everything in
# it diffs. A .pptx is a zip of XML: git can't diff it, and every regeneration
# adds a fresh ~1 MB blob to history permanently.
#
# What this currently keeps out:
#   docs/Demo PPT Template - Octave.pptx        the brand template (belongs in
#                                               Octave's own store, not here)
#   docs/EAM-Dev-Leadership-Deck-2026-08-25.pptx  a meeting artifact, generated
#                                               from EAM-Dev-Leadership-Review-2026-08-25.md
#
# The deck is reproducible from that review doc, which IS tracked — so the
# source of truth is in git even though the binary isn't. If a .pptx ever needs
# committing on purpose, use `git add -f`.
*.pptx
*.potx
*.ppt

# node_modules should never appear here (no build step by design), but a stray
# `npm install` while generating a deck would otherwise leave one behind.
node_modules/
